.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_UNORDERED_INPUT_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_unordered_input_new ,
.Nm dtfl_unordered_input_send ,
.Nm dtfl_unordered_input_flush ,
.Nm dtfl_unordered_input_free
.Nd supply records under caller-managed capabilities
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_new "dtfl_scope *scope" "const dtfl_type *type" \
"dtfl_unordered_input **handle" "dtfl_cap **cap"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_send "dtfl_unordered_input *h" "const dtfl_cap *cap" \
"const void *rec" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_flush "dtfl_unordered_input *h"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_free "dtfl_unordered_input *h"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An unordered input is the capability-based cousin of
.Xr dtfl_input_new 3 :
instead of a single advancing epoch, the caller holds capabilities and
may keep several epochs open at once.
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_new
creates the input operator in
.Fa scope
for records of
.Fa type ,
stores the handle through
.Fa handle ,
and stores an initial capability at the minimum time through
.Fa cap .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_send
sends
.Fa rec
at
.Fa cap Ns 's
time.
The caller controls progress through the capability: obtain a later
capability with
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3
before downgrading or dropping the current one, and drop every
capability to signal end of input.
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_flush
flushes any pending records and activates the operator.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_free
releases the handle.
Capabilities obtained from this input are released separately with
.Xr dtfl_cap_drop 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_unordered_input_new
returns the input stream and stores the handle and the initial
capability through its out-parameters.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_unordered_input *in;
dtfl_cap *cap;
dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_unordered_input_new(scope, dtfl_type_u64(),
    &in, &cap);
dtfl_stream_capture_into(s, pusher, ctx);
/* feed values 0..10 at times 0..10. */
for (uint64_t round = 0; round < 10; round++) {
	unsigned char buf[8];
	uint64_t next = round + 1;
	dtfl_put_u64(buf, round);
	dtfl_unordered_input_send(in, cap, buf, sizeof buf);
	dtfl_cap *later = dtfl_cap_delayed(cap, &next);
	dtfl_cap_drop(cap);
	cap = later;
	dtfl_worker_step(w);
}
dtfl_cap_drop(cap);
dtfl_unordered_input_free(in);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_input_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_probe_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt UnorderedHandle
and the
.Fn new_unordered_input
method of the
.Vt UnorderedInput
trait.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A
.Vt dtfl_unordered_input
and the capabilities it hands out belong to the thread that runs the
worker and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
